  "id": "4f2e0e8f-9e5b-5a28-9902-4216146800dd",
  "slug": "million-dollar-mashed-potatoes-recipe-11849008",
  "name": "Million Dollar Mashed Potatoes",
  "recipe_type": "side",
  "brief_description": "These million dollar mashed potatoes are a little extra, over the top, but oh, so delicious. Enriched with cream cheese, sour cream, Cheddar, and bacon grease for a rich, luscious flavor and mouthfeel, they're creamy and scoopable. Crisp bacon adds a pop of salt, and green onions add a fresh tang.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Place potatoes in a large pot and cover by 1 inch with cold water; bring to a boil over high heat. Reduce heat to medium-high and boil until tender when pierced with a fork, about 15 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Meanwhile, add bacon to a large skillet. Cook over medium-high, stirring often, until browned and crispy, 8 to 11 minutes. Line a plate with paper towels; transfer bacon to the plate using a slotted spoon, and set aside. Reserve 2 tablespoons bacon drippings; set aside."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Drain and return cooked potatoes to pot off the heat, stirring until no water remains, about 1 minute."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Add cream cheese, sour cream, butter, and reserved 2 tablespoons bacon drippings to potatoes and mash with a potato masher until smooth."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Stir in Cheddar cheese, milk, salt, pepper, and 1/2 cup scallions. Season with additional salt."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Garnish with remaining 1/4 cup scallions and reserved bacon. Dollop with sour cream. Recipe developed by Isabelle Easter"
    }
  ],
  "servings": 8,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 35,
  "preparation_time_minutes": 15,
